      "statusChangeNewStatus": "needs more information",
      "value": "The reason this works is not intended behaviour in Unity 2022.3. As such, it is not compatible with Unity 6. If we implement a fix client-side, it would then no longer match editor behaviour for when we provide a Unity 6 SDK, we're hesitant to do that.\n\nAs a workaround, you can simply set the maximum particle count to include those left to be completed, e.g. to 5000 or so. This then realistically reflects the actual maximum amount of particles active, and fixes the issue on Unity 6.\n\nWould this workaround be acceptable for you?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "_id": "6a8e2c9c0e8c4c8b0c099f90",
      "aiGenerated": false,
